  "lawGrade": "PARTIAL",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Heisenberg uncertainty DxDp >= hbar/2; measurement collapses superposition. The mapping: uncertainty <-> the epistemic limit that leaves room for faith; collapse <-> commitment (faith as the engagement that actualizes); complementarity <-> the irreducible tension between divine sovereignty and human freedom. Collapse condition proposed as threshold F*Q >= Theta_c. Canonical status correction: the threshold is a proposed pinning protocol, not a prediction; the F_critical = 0.31-0.35 figure is RETIRED. The F-normalisation defect is open: the earlier P x F formulation broke Born-rule normalization for F > 1; Repair A (basis selection) vs Repair B (renormalisation) awaits David's ruling (OI-0002).",
  "statementPlain": "Quantum systems hold all possibilities until engagement collapses them into one. The proposal: faith is that kind of engagement - not passive uncertainty but the commitment that actualizes. Canon is blunt about the state of play: the collapse threshold is a proposed protocol, not a prediction; the old threshold numbers are retired; and the math of how faith enters the amplitude broke once already and remains open pending a repair ruling. The physics is established; the faith mapping is partial and not proven.",
  "mathematicalForm": "DxDp >= hbar/2; proposed collapse condition: F*Q >= Theta_c => |Phi> -> |outcome> (pinning protocol, not prediction)",
  "mathFormNormal": "DxDp >= hbar/2; proposed collapse condition: F*Q >= Theta_c => |Phi> -> |outcome> (pinning protocol, not prediction)",
